==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Fisherman Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Doctor Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Initially, Fortune Teller Cat is a very potent counter to [[Shy Boy]], most [[Teacher Bun Bun]] variants, [[Red Cyclone]], [[Dark Cyclone]] and [[White Cyclone]]. Due to their very low range, Fortune Teller's frequent attacks can easily keep them at bay.

Later in the game, his ability becomes more risky as more stages include backline enemies who can kill any cat that enters that range. It is recommended to replace him with [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] or [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necro-Dancer Cat]], as the former has Area Attack and both have safer abilities (Slow/Freeze) and superior range.

Although he becomes obsolete rather easily, the one thing he can be used for at any point in the game is [[Moby Dick (Combo)|Moby Dick]], a Unit Defense Up (Sm) [[Cat Combo]] which also activates [[Cap'n Ahab (Combo)|Cap'n Ahab]].

==='''True Form'''===
Doctor Cat gains a 10% increased chance to knockback Floating enemies and doubled health. This relatively minor improvement, compared to its peers, makes unlocking this form a low priority unless you also aim to unlock his talents. Despite everything, it can be useful for stages like [[Tiny Wings (Deadly)|Tiny Wings]], when you don't have many other reliable options for controlling [[Li'l Flying Cat (Enemy)|Li'l Flying Cat]], as it has very high range and only one Knockback, making his Knockback ability much more valuable whenever if the other enemies aren't around.

Against all odds, this unit also works surprisingly well in [[Mega Menace/On Mighty Wings Lv1~20|Mega Menace]].

==='''Talents'''===
His Target [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] [[Talents|Talent]] allows him to quite safely keep [[Oldhorn]] and [[Primeval Cyclone]] at bay. It also allows him to stun-lock certain Relic bosses by their base, making them useless (notably, when used properly, a group of Doctor Cats can completely stunlock the [[Zero Luza|final boss]] of Uncanny Legends), plus it can shake off certain enemies from the Cat Base, such as [[Ultima Beast Naala|Naala]]. Health Up and Resist Curse slightly improve Doctor's chances at delivering one last knockback after taking a hit, but they are hardly worth it if this cat is not boosted. Finally, Attack Up and Resist Knockback are nigh-useless, as Doctor Cat is not used for his damage, and Knockback Resist hinders his survivability.

==='''Orb'''===
Using any Effect orb on Doctor Cat would likely be a waste, but if one needs to be chosen, it should be a health up for Floating. Remember that [[Catseye]]s and + levels are better ways to improve this unit's survivability.

A-grade curse resist orb with same talent unlocked for immunity.

