==Trivia==
*[[Version 2.0 Update#Version 2.0.6 Update|Version 2.0.6]] increased Fortune Teller Cat's knockback chance from 10% to 30%.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Fortune Teller Cat was a part of another [[Cat Combo]] called [[Medium Cool (Removed Combo)|Medium Cool]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Fortune Teller Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Fortune Teller Cat
A Cat that loves the idea of fortune telling.
Has read one too many astrology books.
Might knockback Floating enemies.</pre>
<pre>Fisherman Cat
Eldest son of a prominent
Tuna fisherman. Gets seasick.
Might knockback Floating enemies.</pre>
<pre>Doctor Cat
His medical philosophy is "Hair of the Dog".
If it doesn't kill ya, it must be working, right?!
Might knockback Floating enemies.</pre>
*Fisherman Cat's Japanese written on Fisherman's loincloth, 海人, is the word for a male diver or fisherman.
*The "[[wikipedia:Hair of the dog|hair of the dog]]" philosophy mentioned in Doctor Cat's English description refers to alcohol taken to remedy a hangover.
*Doctor Cat is likely a reference to [[mariowiki:Doctor Mario|Doctor Mario]].
*In [[The Battle Cats POP!]], Fortune Teller Cat was named Mystic Cat.

